== Abstract ==

This BIP defines the derivation scheme for HD wallets which create timelocked addresses used for creating fidelity bonds. It also gives advice to wallet developers on how to use fidelity bonds to sign over messages, such as certificates, which are needed when using fidelity bonds that are stored offline.

Two versions of the scheme are defined: Version 1, the original scheme already deployed in JoinMarket, and Version 2, a revision using a dedicated derivation <tt>purpose</tt> and a Miniscript-compatible <tt>witness script</tt>. Wallets SHOULD create new fidelity bonds using Version 2, and SHOULD also recognize Version 1 fidelity bonds that already exist.

